# NOTE ON WHAT IS AND IS NOT IGNORED HERE.
#
# public/models/* is what the site SERVES, so none of it is ignored: the hero
# cannot render without it and a clone of this repo has to be able to build and
# deploy on its own. 7.3 MB of binaries, which is deliberate. Rebuild with:
#   /Applications/Blender.app/Contents/MacOS/Blender -b assets/cad/xuanyiji_master.blend -P scripts/build-cad-layers.py
#
# It was 18 MB until the teardown moved off the 3DGS captures onto the CAD. The
# gaussian payloads and the point cloud the wordmark used to be downloaded from
# are gone; the hero now derives its particles from the same meshes it draws.
#
# What IS ignored below is the two large SOURCE inputs. Neither lives outside this
# folder — nothing in the project reads a path outside it — but neither belongs in
# git history at its size, and neither is needed to build or serve the site, only
# to regenerate the binaries above. Use Git LFS if the sources should be versioned.

# Source 3DGS captures, ~80 MB. Nothing on the site reads these any more; they are
# the input to scripts/build-layers.mjs, which no longer feeds anything.
# See assets/captures/README.md.
/assets/captures/cleanply/

# Source CAD, ~233 MB. See assets/cad/README.md.
/assets/cad/*.blend
/assets/cad/*.blend[0-9]

# Python bytecode from the Blender-side build scripts.
__pycache__/

# Precompressed copies of the model binaries, written by scripts/precompress.mjs
# from `prebuild` and served by src/app/hero-model/[file]/route.ts. Derived bytes:
# 4 MB of brotli plus 5 MB of gzip beside a 7.3 MB source is three copies of one
# asset in git history, and `npm run build` regenerates them in 21 s.
/public/models/*.br
/public/models/*.gz
